"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1KFTFVQTY1S08RE0\",\"title\":\"Carboneyes: Udongo — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"Carboneyes: Udongo\",\"Carboneyes\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2027\",\"Project code\",\"PHZ6\",\"Crediting period\",\"01 Oct 2026 to 01 Oct 2031\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"PHZ6\",\"approval\":\"Expected 2027\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"19 Jun 2026\",\"Public Comment Period Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"20 May 2026\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://carboneyes.co\",\"t\":\"Carboneyes\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.3\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.3\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1K5S032D11S0PW0K\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-requirements\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1KOmLuhU6yzCYYtUWPyQCw4aByEEJ7Q1-/view\",\"t\":\"VVB Policy\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K5S032D11S0PW0K/prj_1KFTFVQTY1S08RE0/pjd_1KVFFFBK61S0WDCK/public_comment_period_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1K5S032D11S0PW0K/prj_1KFTFVQTY1S08RE0/pjd_1KS2RDS091S0YBAT/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nCarboneyes: Udongo\\nCarboneyes\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2027\\nProject code\\nPHZ6\\nCrediting period\\n01 Oct 2026 to 01 Oct 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.3\\nSummary\\n\\nBagasse is the fibrous residue remaining after sugarcane is crushed for sugar production. A single mill can generate hundreds of thousands of tonnes per year. A portion is used for on-site cogeneration and briquetting, but even at full capacity a significant surplus remains. This surplus is disposed of in open heaps where it decomposes under partially anaerobic conditions, releasing CO₂ and methane, and producing acidic leachate that can contaminate surrounding soils and waterways. Project Udongo converts the surplus bagasse into biochar through pyrolysis at a facility co-located on the mill site. The biochar is donated free of charge to smallholder sugarcane farmers, alongside training, to deliver durable carbon removal whilst improving soil health, reducing fertiliser dependence and building climate resilience in local communities.\\n\\nKenya\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 29 May 2026\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2026\\nInitial documentation submission\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nAudit kick-off\\n\\nA Validation & Verification Body (VVB) officially commences the project validation and verification process. All VVBs are approved and appointed by Isometric based on the requirements outlined in the Isometric Standard and VVB Policy.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2027\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2027\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n19 Jun 2026\\tPublic Comment Period Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n20 May 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"